  "notes": "Transcribed from the official Loma Linda University 2026-2027 Catalog (effective Summer Quarter 2026) program page 'Radiation Therapy Technology - B.S.' (School of Allied Health Professions, Department of Radiation Technology), ARRT-certified-students track. The catalog publishes the curriculum split by 7 quarters; quarter sums verified: Y1 Autumn: 15, Y1 Winter: 15, Y1 Spring: 16, Y2 Summer: 14, Y2 Autumn: 13, Y2 Winter: 16, Y2 Spring: 11 = 100 = the curriculum table's Total Units 100. Note: the page's prerequisite text states students 'will earn 96 units in the program,' which is inconsistent with the official curriculum table (Total Units: 100); the table is transcribed because it is internally consistent and authoritative for the sequence. Footnote 1: the CT sequence (RTSI 364, RTSI 367, RTSI 369) may be substituted with the CT sequence completed by LLU's ASMR students (RTMR 305, RTMR 306, RTSI 307). RELT 415 may be substituted with another RELR course per catalog note; encoded with that option. RTCH 492 (Portfolio II) fulfills the service learning requirement per footnote 2. program_type 'professional-phase': the program is intended for radiographers or other allied health professionals seeking additional specialization (ARRT-certified entrants), and the LLU portion is the 7-quarter professional phase after 96 quarter units of prerequisites. Non-ARRT students take an additional first Summer Quarter (radiation physics, radiation protection, principles of radiography, patient care methods) per the catalog, but no tabulated curriculum is published for that variant, so it is documented here rather than encoded. The only per-course prerequisite stated in the catalog is RTTH 365 (requires RTTH 364); the remaining published quarter order is the official sequence, so other prereq arrays are intentionally empty. Normal time to complete: 4 years including prerequisites (LLU portion: 7 quarters / 21 months), full-time enrollment.",
